[=#oracledateformat]
= Date Format =

Oracle clients expect DATE columns to include the time of day, but an Oracle back-end's default date format usually drops it.  To keep it, set the //date_to_text_format// parameter in the connection tag's connect string (see the [../configreference.html#oracle Configuration Reference]), for example:

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
<connection string="user=exampleuser;password=examplepassword;oracle_sid=ora1;date_to_text_format=YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS"/>
}}}
}}}

DATE columns are then returned in that format.  TIMESTAMP columns, and how dates in queries are parsed, are unaffected.  Use a numeric, fixed-width format, with only /, - and : as delimiters, like the one above, or the date may not be parsed correctly.  Also make sure //maxfieldsize//, if set, is large enough not to truncate it.

----

